---
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';

export const title = 'Keyboard and events';
export const order = 600;
---
<p>
  The accordion is one tab stop. <kbd>Up</kbd> and <kbd>Down</kbd> move focus
  between the panel headers, <kbd>Home</kbd> and <kbd>End</kbd> jump to the
  first and last; disabled panels are skipped. <kbd>Enter</kbd> or
  <kbd>Space</kbd> opens or closes the focused panel.
</p>
<p>
  Each <code>wc-accordion-item</code> fires <code>open</code> after it expands
  and <code>close</code> after it collapses. Both bubble and carry
  <code>detail.reason</code>: <code>'action'</code> when the person used the
  header, <code>'api'</code> when <code>open</code> was set, or
  <code>show()</code>, <code>hide()</code> or <code>toggle()</code> was called
  (including when a single-panel accordion closes the others).
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={"html"}>
  <wc-accordion>
    <wc-accordion-item>
      <span slot="heading">Panel A</span>
      <p>Content for panel A.</p>
    </wc-accordion-item>
    <wc-accordion-item>
      <span slot="heading">Panel B</span>
      <p>Content for panel B.</p>
    </wc-accordion-item>
  </wc-accordion>
</DemoComponentCard>

<pre><code>{`accordion.addEventListener('open', event => {
  console.log(event.target, event.detail.reason);
});`}</code></pre>

<h3>Deprecated</h3>
<p>
  The <code>accordion-item-toggle</code> event still fires when the person opens
  or closes a panel, but is deprecated: listen for <code>open</code> and
  <code>close</code>. 4.0 removes it.
</p>
